{
  "schema": 1,
  "name": "Bloodmage Night Hunter's Howl, Aortic Assault and Mortal Form abilities scale with their tooltip stats",
  "contract": [
    "Every rank's client tooltip advertises its coefficient as a description token, with EffectBonusMultiplier 0:",
    "Night Hunter's Howl ${$m1+0+$AP*0.285}; Aortic Assault strikes ${$m1+0+$AP*0.12} (strike 806502) and",
    "ends with ${$806214m1+$806214ppl1+$AP*0.6} (finale 806214); Veinburst ${$m1+0+$AP*.25+$sps*0.85)};",
    "Crimson Tide ($m1+0+$SP*.28) per tick; Scarlet Delirium siphons ${$m2+0+$SP*0.15} every $t2 sec;",
    "Vampiric Fang ${$m1+0+$SP*0.34}; Dark Liturgy heals ${$m1+0+$SP*0.35+$SPI*0.25};",
    "Sanguine Mend heals ${$m1+0+$SPI*0.25+$AP*.2+$SP*.58}.",
    "The AP and SP coefficients reach Unit::SpellDamageBonusDone and Unit::SpellHealingBonusDone only through",
    "spell_bonus_data, looked up by the first rank, so the level-56 to level-60 ranks tested here also prove",
    "the rank fallback; at level 60 they carry no level penalty, and the Aortic Assault spells have none.",
    "spell_damage_done and spell_healing_done use a fixed base of 1000, so the gain after +1000 attack power",
    "(10031), +2000 spell damage to every school (44505) and +2000 bonus healing (QATest 51041) measures each",
    "coefficient. The Spirit terms are base-value bonuses, measured with spell_effect_value after +1000 Spirit",
    "(QA Test 486). That value includes the effect's die roll (Dark Liturgy 23 sides, Sanguine Mend 52), so two",
    "snapshots can differ by up to DieSides - 1 points, and each Spirit window spans that over a 900 Spirit gain."
  ],
